    description: "Found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- py_def_use.py: The docstring line \"Delete: ``del x`` -> defines [x]\" (L26) holds only for a single bare identifier. `_handle_delete` (L364-370) collects only direct `identifier` children (it is registered at L442 `\"delete_statement\": _handle_delete`). Repro (tree-sitter-language-pack python parser through `_handle_delete`):\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # c5ad
